      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T00:17:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems quite error prone?  It requires any (new) client to remember adding a random header file before they include the targeting ones (e.g. vm_payload_restricted.h here).  What would be a more scalable solution?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4f9fb961307c3b57e4c84537d94ac159971800b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04be5a4c_c13eb39d",
        "filename": "compos/compos_key_helper/compos_key_main.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T00:21:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The other solution I had in mind was to remove the include to stdnoreturn.h and use _Noreturn (or __attribute__((noreturn))) instead. I am not certain how it fares on all archs/platforms though.\n\nLet me know what you prefer?",
      "parentUuid": "f6d0e81b_bd0e2857",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4f9fb961307c3b57e4c84537d94ac159971800b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c60e7cf_2e110ed8",
        "filename": "compos/compos_key_helper/compos_key_main.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T00:30:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess I also don\u0027t really understand the problem here.  If it conflicts with stdnoreturn.h, why including format.h here instead of the header with stdnoreturn.h?",
      "parentUuid": "04be5a4c_c13eb39d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4f9fb961307c3b57e4c84537d94ac159971800b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76dc479b_8f4c6382",
        "filename": "compos/compos_key_helper/compos_key_main.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T00:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens is, the preprocessor will expand the following:\n```\n#include \u003cvm_payload_restricted.h\u003e\n-\u003e #include \u003cstdnoreturn.h\u003e \n----\u003e #define noreturn _Noreturn\n\n#include \"compos_key.h\"\n-\u003e #include \u003candroid-base/result.h\u003e\n----\u003e #include \u003cfmt/std.h\u003e\n-------\u003e #include \u003ccxxabi.h\u003e\n-----------\u003e uses __attribute__((noreturn))\n```\n\nBecause `noreturn` is defined by `\u003cstdnoreturn.h\u003e` to `_Noreturn`, it gets replaced in `__attribute__((noreturn))`, which causes an `unknown attribute` compilation error.\n\nBy force-including \u003candroid-format.h\u003e before \u003cvm_payload_restricted.h\u003e, I ensure that the noreturn definition does no conflict.",
      "parentUuid": "7c60e7cf_2e110ed8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4f9fb961307c3b57e4c84537d94ac159971800b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
